G5119.def:
τότε, demonstr. adv. of time, correlat. of ὅτε, 
then, at that time; 
__(a) of concurrent events: Matthieu 2:17 3:5 and freq., Romains 6:21; before ptcp., Matthieu 2:16, Galates 4:8; opposite to νῦν, Galates 4:29, Hébreux 12:26; ὁ τ. κόσμος, 2 Pierre 3:6; 
__(b) of consequent events, then, thereupon: Matthieu 2:7 3:5 4:1 and freq., Luc 11:26; τ. οὖν, Jean 11:14 19:1, 16 20:8; εὐθέως τ., Actes 17:14; ὅτε . . . τ., Matthieu 13:26 21:1, Jean 12:16; ἀπὸ τ., Matthieu 4:17 16:21 26:16, Luc 16:16; 
__(with) of things future: Matthieu 24:28, 40 25:1, 31ff.; opposite to ἄρτι, 1 Corinthiens 13:12; καὶ τ., Matthieu 7:23, Marc 13:21, Luc 21:27, 1 Corinthiens 4:5, al.; ὅταν . . . τ., Matthieu 9:15, Marc 2:20, Luc 5:35, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:3, al. (more frequently in Mt than in the rest of the NT).

G5192.def:
ὑακίνθος, -ου, ό 
[in LXX chiefly for תְּכֵלֶת ;] 
hyacinth; 
__(a) in cl., a flower, prob. the dark blue iris; 
__(b) in late writers, a precious stone of the same colour, perhaps the sapphire: Apocalypse 21:20 (Phil., FlJ, al.).†
